# CAPTURES — inspect capture activity, diagnostics, retry or clear failed captures.
# See README.md for environments and labels.
#
# Copy the workflowInstanceId from request 1 or 2 into @failureId before running 3, 4 or 5.

@failureId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 1. READ ONLY — Capture activity (preparing, indexing, enriching, and failed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/captures/activity
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### 2. READ ONLY — Active failed captures
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/captures/failures
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### 3. READ ONLY — Failure diagnostics (error and stack trace)
# @failureId is the workflowInstanceId from request 1 or 2.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/captures/failures/{{failureId}}/details
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### 4. START + AI — Retry a failed capture
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/captures/failures/{{failureId}}/retry
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### 5. DESTRUCTIVE — Clear a failed capture and queue residue cleanup
# Returns 409 NOT_FAILED_CAPTURE if the workflow is not in a failed state with a failed task.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/captures/failures/{{failureId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
